course: dictionary
lesson: 11606
title: Appointed: chosen, fixed, or well equipped
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Appointed is the past form of the verb appoint, so it often describes someone being chosen for a job. «The school appointed a new head teacher in May.» The clue is the job: a head teacher is a role someone is given officially, so appointed means chosen for that role.
explain: Appointed can also be an adjective that means fixed or agreed. «We met at the appointed time, at three o'clock.» Time is the clue here. The meeting was arranged in advance, so appointed means the time that was agreed.
explain: In a formal sentence, appointed can describe a room or place. «The hotel room was well-appointed, with soft beds and a big desk.» Well-appointed means well equipped and nicely furnished. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Appointed is the past form of the verb appoint, so it means someone was chosen or given a job.
fact: «Appointed» can also mean fixed or agreed, as in «the appointed time».
fact: «Well-appointed» means well equipped and nicely furnished.
fact: Clues such as a job, a time, or a room help you find the meaning of appointed.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The school appointed Mrs Lee as head teacher.» What does appointed mean here? | Thrown out of the school | *Chosen officially for the job | Painted in bright colours | Lost somewhere
exercise: «We met at the appointed time, at three o'clock.» What does appointed mean here? | Secret | Broken | *Fixed or agreed | Late
exercise: «The hotel room was well-appointed, with soft beds and a big desk.» What does well-appointed mean? | *Well equipped and nicely furnished | Closed for repairs | Very dirty and messy | Too small to use
test: «Sam was appointed monitor for the library.» Who was chosen for the job of library monitor? | Nobody, the job was cancelled | The whole class together | The librarian's cat | *Sam
test: Mum says, «Be at the door at the appointed hour.» What does appointed hour mean? | The hour when school closes early | *The time that was agreed | An hour of free play | An hour that nobody remembers
exam: «The council appointed a new leader, and everyone agreed on the appointed day.» Which meaning fits appointed in each part? | Late, then secret | Painted, then cleaned | *Chosen for a job, then fixed or agreed | Lost, then broken
